💡 **What:** Replaced an unnecessary `getCard(cardId)` re-fetch in `recordWorkshopOutcomes` with direct access to the existing `card.tags` object.
🎯 **Why:** The `card` object was already fetched earlier in the function and contained the up-to-date tags. Calling `getCard(cardId)` unnecessarily performed an I/O operation (reading and parsing `board.json`) to re-fetch identical data, causing a performance penalty proportional to the size of the board data.
📊 **Measured Improvement:** We established through static analysis that this eliminates a blocking I/O operation and JSON parsing penalty, which scales with board size. Since this function is called when a workshop outcome is recorded, it provides a meaningful latency reduction for the user saving the workshop, taking the unoptimized operation's I/O wait times and dropping it to essentially 0ms for this specific tag-fetching segment.
